course: dictionary
lesson: 15487
title: One word, many meanings: struck
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Struck is the past form of the verb strike, so it tells you about something that has already happened. Strike is a word with many meanings, so context tells you which one is right.
explain: «The lightning struck the old oak tree.» The sentence is about a storm and a tree, so struck means hit suddenly. Try your meaning in the sentence: the lightning hit the old oak tree. It still makes sense.
explain: «The clock struck midnight.» Here struck means rang a bell to show the time, not hit. «An idea struck Mia.» Here struck means came suddenly into her mind. The words around struck always give you the clue.
fact: Struck is the past form of strike: strike, strikes, struck, striking.
fact: «Struck» can mean hit something hard, as in «The ship struck a rock.»
fact: «Struck» can mean lightning hit something, as in «Lightning struck the tree.»
fact: «Struck» can mean a clock rang to show the time, as in «The clock struck three.»
fact: «Struck» can mean an idea or feeling came suddenly, as in «It struck me that I had left my book at school.»
exercise: «The ship struck a rock and began to sink.» What does struck mean here? | Lit a light | *Hit something hard | Rang a bell | Came into mind
exercise: «The clock struck six, so it was time for tea.» What does struck mean here? | *Rang to show the time | Lit up brightly | Hit someone hard | Came suddenly to mind
exercise: «Mum struck a match to light the candle.» What did Mum do? | *Lit a match by rubbing it | Stopped work as a protest | Rang a bell | Hit the candle
test: «An idea struck Sam in the bath: he could build a boat from cardboard.» What does struck mean here? | Rang a bell | Hit hard | Lit a match | *Came suddenly into his mind
test: «The workers struck to protest about their pay.» What does struck mean here? | Hit the ground | Rang to show the time | Lit up | *Stopped work as a protest
exam: «Lightning struck a tall tree during the storm.» What should you do if you hear thunder nearby? | Go down to the water to watch | *Go indoors and stay away from tall trees and water | Stand under the tallest tree to stay dry | Stand on the hill and wave an umbrella
